  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advancing IOM&#x2019;S Global Data Institute: Disaggregating Migration Data by Sex/Gender to Leave No One Behind</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Data Institute (GDI) unites IOM&#x2019;s Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) &amp; Global Migration Analysis Centre (GMDAC) in comprehensive effort to promote gender-responsive migration data aligned with global development goals and UN strategies. The initiative, spanning two phases over 24 months, aims to enhance data collection, analysis, and utilization to ensure inclusivity in migration policies and practices. 
 
In Phase 1 (Jan to Jun 2023), the focus is on developing tools, guidance materials, and workshops to support governments in Africa and beyond to collect gender-disaggregated migration data effectively. This involves collaboration with partners like UN Women and engagement with regional bodies such as the African Union. 
 
Phase 2 (Jul 2023 to Dec 2024) targets three governments to strengthen gender-responsive migration data through tailored workshops and technical support. The initiative also extends to emergency response data through the Enhancement of Emergency Tracking Tool, emphasizing sex- and age-disaggregated data collection to better understand displacement dynamics. 
 
The GDI&apos;s approach is rooted in human rights and gender equality principles, aligning with international and regional frameworks like the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development and the African Union&apos;s migration policies. GDI aims to leave no one behind in migration governance, contributing to more informed and inclusive policies globally.</narrative>
  </description>
